<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo in $30 mln Uzbekistan expansion.</title>
<headline>Daewoo in $30 mln Uzbekistan expansion.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Electronics Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Daewoo Group, said on Monday it had invested $30 million to expand production of colour televisions and video cassette recorders (VCRs) in Uzbekistan.</p>
<p>Daewoo said in a statement that its annual colour TV output in the country would rise to 300,000 from the current 100,000 and its annual VCR capacity to 200,000 from 100,000 when the new production lines start operation at the end of July.</p>
<p>The Uzbekistan plant was set up in September 1993 in a joint venture with Uzautop Rom.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
